## 132. Figure Counting Master Table

| Figure | Main method |
|---|---|
| Line segment | Choose 2 points |
| Square grid | Sum square sizes |
| Rectangle grid | Choose boundary lines |
| Triangle | Size + orientation + combinations |
| Quadrilateral | Boundary/path method |
| Circle | Complete circular boundaries |
| Polygon | Count valid closed boundaries |
| Intersections | Pairwise line intersections |
| Regions | Partition analysis |
| Complex | Vertex-edge graph |

---

## 133. Advanced Triangle Counting Formula Warning

There are formulas for special triangular grids, but **do not use a memorized formula unless the diagram exactly matches its assumptions**.

For arbitrary diagrams:

```text
\boxed{\text{Manual structural counting is safer}}
```

---

## 134. Why Memorization Can Fail

Two diagrams can both look triangular but have different:

- internal lines
- orientations
- intersections
- spacing
- subdivisions

Therefore they can have completely different triangle counts.

---

## 135. Best Strategy for Exam

```text
REGULAR GRID
→ Formula

IRREGULAR FIGURE
→ Label + Count

COMPLEX CROSSING
→ Graph/vertex method

TRIANGLE MESH
→ Size + orientation table

SYMMETRIC FIGURE
→ Half-count + center check
```

---

## 136. 30-Second Verification

After calculating:

```text
1. Did I count small?
2. Did I count medium?
3. Did I count large?
4. Did I count inverted?
5. Did I count composite?
6. Did I count outer?
7. Did I double-count?
```

---

## 137. Final Universal Algorithm

```text
                 DIAGRAM
                    │
                    ▼
             Mark all vertices
                    │
                    ▼
             Identify all edges
                    │
                    ▼
        ┌───────────┼───────────┐
        ▼           ▼           ▼
      SMALL       MEDIUM       LARGE
        │           │           │
        └───────────┼───────────┘
                    ▼
             Check combinations
                    │
                    ▼
             Check orientation
                    │
                    ▼
             Check outer figure
                    │
                    ▼
              Remove duplicates
                    │
                    ▼
                   TOTAL
```

